C.3:
PASS-equivalent (design choice): no generic `write_cdp_blocked_result` function. Instead:
  - `cdp_blocked_sizing_result(row)` exists at main.rs:12380 for the shipment-sizing typed result.
  - For other skills, the daemon's preflight (`preflight_cdp_for_skill`, `preflight_cdp_for_launch_spec`)
    logs a warning and lets the skill body detect CDP down via its own ensure-cdp-9222 invocation
    and write the blocked result. See main.rs:12353 comment:
    "skill will see CDP down and write its own blocked result"

The handoff anticipated a different implementation; the actual daemon uses a "preflight-and-warn"
approach combined with skill-level defense-in-depth (which Area B verified is in place). No fix needed.

